# <%= title %>

Built with [Abqari](https://github.com/grantrayner/abqari) — a Ruby static
site generator. The engine handles content pipelines, layouts, helpers,
themes, and the build orchestrator; everything in this repo is YOUR
site's content, configuration, and assets.

## Quick start

```bash
bundle install
bin/serve              # dev server on http://localhost:4000
```

When you're ready to ship:

```bash
bin/build              # production build → _site/
bin/audit              # link / SEO / a11y / privacy checks
```

## Day-to-day

```bash
bin/new post "Title"   # scaffold a new post bundle in content/posts/
bin/new page "Title"   # scaffold a top-level page in content/
```

To enable another collection (photos, publications, workshops) after
the fact: flip its `enabled:` flag in `config/site.yml` and create
`content/<name>/index.md` — the comments in the config show the shape.
(`abqari new --with <name>` does both for fresh sites.)

## Where to edit

| Path | What lives here |
|---|---|
| `config/site.yml` | Site identity, theme, collections, home modules, env overrides |
| `content/` | Markdown — posts, pages, photos, publications, workshops |
| `app/assets/css/site.css` | Your custom CSS (loads after the theme; never overwritten by upgrades) |
| `data/` | YAML/JSON data files exposed to templates as `site.data['name']` |
| `public/` | Static passthrough — favicons, robots overrides, etc. |

## Upgrading the engine

Bundler reads the Gemfile each time it runs. To pull engine updates:

```bash
bundle update abqari
bin/build              # confirm the build still passes
bin/audit              # confirm content audit still passes
```

See the engine's [CHANGELOG](https://github.com/grantrayner/abqari/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)
for what changed between versions and whether any of your config or
content needs a migration.

